\node Test, ANVL Test Plugin
@chapter Test, ANVL Plugin

@code{anvl_test} is a plugin for running Erlang/OTP test suites.

Test suites are discovered automatically in the OTP applications of the
project, and executed on isolated peer nodes.

@section Writing test suites

A test suite is an Erlang module that implements the
@code{anvl_test_suite} behavior:

@verbatim
-module(my_suite).
-behavior(anvl_test_suite).

-include_lib("anvl_test/include/anvl_test.hrl").

-test(some_test).
some_test(run, #{instance := _}) ->
  ok.
@end verbatim

Including @file{anvl_test.hrl} applies a parse transform that collects
the @code{-test} attributes into a module attribute
(@code{anvl_test_tests}) and exports the test functions.

@section Test case instances

The same test function can be run against multiple @i{instances}.
Default implementation of the @code{instances/0} callback returns
@code{[default]}.

@lee{anvl_test,ANVL Test}
